digraph ReasoningTree {
  // paper_id=s41467-025-56757-2
  rankdir="TB";
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes and motivates a nano-CMDO approach based on a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor: a perpendicular electric field orients dipolar conjugated-polymer backbones while alkyl-modified plates assist side-chain alignment, aiming to form high-quality single-crystal thin films with ultralow energetic disorder and high charge-carrier mobility.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A controlled nanoconfined electrostatic environment can be investigated as a way to overcome limitations of conventional conjugated-polymer thin-film crystallization by coordinating backbone rotation, side-chain alignment, and crystal growth."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) Conjugated polymers are scientifically relevant materials for advanced and wearable electronics because their molecular diversity, electronic versatility, and mechanical flexibility align with applications such as OECT-based circuitry."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Because accelerated nucleation can lead to polycrystalline grains, controlling molecular dipoles is nontrivial, especially since molecular dipoles are highly sensitive to molecular configurations and stacking conformations."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) External-force approaches such as fluid-flow alignment can arrange polymer chains, but these approaches are constrained by limited nanoscopic control over twisted molecular configurations."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Together, limited nanoscopic control by external-force alignment and the configuration sensitivity of molecular dipoles motivate the view that balancing localized molecular rotations with comprehensive chain alignment remains difficult in thin-film conjugated-polymer crystallization."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) To address the difficulty of balancing localized molecular rotations and chain alignment, it is reasonable to develop and evaluate a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor that uses a perpendicular electric field to rotate conjugated-polymer backbones through molecular dipoles while alkyl-modified plates align side chains."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) For conjugated polymers used in advanced thin-film electronics, their semiconducting capabilities depend substantially on long-range delocalization of electronic wave functions across polymer chains."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) Single-crystal conjugated-polymer thin films are an ideal platform for studying and exploiting long-range electronic delocalization because their ordered conformations and stacking can support intermolecular charge transport."];
  "R4" [label="(0,0,0) Although single-crystal conjugated-polymer films are desirable, manufacturing CP single crystals remains significantly challenging because energetic preference and entropic chain motion can conflict during crystallization."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) The difficulty of manufacturing conjugated-polymer single crystals is further exacerbated in thin films, where two-dimensional constraints limit polymer-chain freedom to reach favorable crystalline arrangements."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) The thin-film crystallization challenge motivates investigating localized molecular dipoles in conjugated polymers as possible handles for modulating crystallization behavior."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) When molecular dipoles are investigated as crystallization handles, they may thermodynamically modulate the energy landscape of pi-pi stacking and lower barriers toward ordered states."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) If molecular dipoles serve as modulators of conjugated-polymer crystallization, they are also expected to kinetically accelerate nucleation by fostering highly ordered initial states and more uniform crystal growth."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Accelerated nucleation driven by molecular-dipole effects may create a risk of high-density random nuclei, producing polycrystalline films with abundant grains."];
  "challenge_rule" [label="(4,0,0) If single crystals are ideal platform, then the manufacturing of CP single crystals remains significantly challenging, mainly ascribed to the intrinsic contradiction between the energetic preference and the entropic cost for organizing random polymer chains into well-ordered arrangements."];
  "deloc_rule" [label="(2,0,0) If conjugated polymers are pioneering in advanced thin-film electronics, then their semiconducting capabilities are essentially determined by long-range delocalization of electronic wave functions across polymer chains."];
  "drawback_rule" [label="(9,0,0) If molecular dipoles accelerate the nucleation, then unfortunately accelerated nucleation is often accompanied by high-density random crystal nuclei leading to polycrystals with abundant grains."];
  "exacerbated_rule" [label="(5,0,0) If the manufacturing is challenging, then this challenge is further exacerbated in thin films, where two-dimensional constraints limit the spatial freedom of chains to arrange into the energetically favorable crystalline state, and the π-π stackings along two-dimensional scales are more easily disrupted by molecular irregularities, thermal agitations, and mechanical detachments."];
  "explore_knowledge" [label="(6,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: Electronegativity differences between carbon and heteroatoms create localized molecular dipoles due to the asymmetric distribution of electrons."];
  "external_ind_case" [label="(11,1,1) Induction-case: External forces such as fluid flow have been employed for aligned arrangements of polymer chains."];
  "external_ind_common" [label="(11,0,0) Induction-common: These approaches are constrained by the lack of nanoscopic controls over twisted molecular configurations."];
  "final_knowledge" [label="(14,0,0) Abduction-knowledge: Rational design of spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor allows molecular dipoles to rotate conjugated backbones in response to a perpendicular electric field while alkyl-modified parallel plates are engineered to regulate side chains."];
  "ideal_rule" [label="(3,0,0) If the semiconducting capabilities of CPs are essentially determined by long-range delocalization of electronic wave functions across polymer chains, then single crystals characterized by perfect coplanar conformations, minimum energetic disorders, and enhanced carrier mobility have been widely recognized as an ideal platform to access peak semiconducting performances and explore inherent structure-property relationships."];
  "ind_case" [label="(1,1,6) Induction-case: There is a case where OECTs and OECT-based circuitry offer great potential in wearable electronics."];
  "ind_common" [label="(1,0,0) Induction-common: Conjugated polymers have a unique combination of molecular diversity, electronic versatility, and mechanical flexibility."];
  "kinetic_rule" [label="(8,0,0) If molecular dipoles serve as modulators, then on the kinetic front molecular dipoles are expected to accelerate the nucleation by fostering highly-ordered initial states and contribute to more uniform and rapid crystal growths."];
  "sensitivity_rule" [label="(10,0,0) If accelerated nucleation leads to polycrystals, then in addition molecular dipoles are highly sensitive to both molecular configurations and stacking conformations."];
  "thermo_rule" [label="(7,0,0) If we explore molecular dipoles, then from the thermodynamic perspective molecular dipoles may serve as subtle modulators to influence the energy landscape of π-π stackings, thus lowering the energy barrier towards a single-crystal state."];
  "ind_case" -> "R1" [label="induction-case"];
  "ind_common" -> "R1" [label="induction-common"];
  "deloc_rule" -> "R2" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R1" -> "R2" [label="deduction-case"];
  "ideal_rule" -> "R3" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R2" -> "R3" [label="deduction-case"];
  "challenge_rule" -> "R4" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R3" -> "R4" [label="deduction-case"];
  "exacerbated_rule" -> "R5" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R4" -> "R5" [label="deduction-case"];
  "R5" -> "R6" [label="abduction-phenomenon"];
  "explore_knowledge" -> "R6" [label="abduction-knowledge"];
  "thermo_rule" -> "R7" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R6" -> "R7" [label="deduction-case"];
  "kinetic_rule" -> "R8" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R7" -> "R8" [label="deduction-case"];
  "drawback_rule" -> "R9" [label="deduction-rule"];
  "R8" -> "R9" [label="deduction-case"];
